findings.remediation:
If the load balancer must be internet-facing, attach a WAFv2 Web ACL and keep
listeners on HTTPS only. Otherwise make it internal:
resource "aws_lb" "this" {
  internal = true
  # ...
}

Replace the HTTP listener with HTTPS. Create an ACM certificate and attach it:
resource "aws_lb_listener" "https" {
  load_balancer_arn = aws_lb.this.arn
  port              = 443
  protocol          = "HTTPS"
  ssl_policy        = "ELBSecurityPolicy-TLS13-1-2-2021-06"
  certificate_arn   = aws_acm_certificate.this.arn
  default_action { type = "forward" target_group_arn = aws_lb_target_group.this.arn }
}
Add an HTTP listener that redirects to HTTPS (301).

Enable deletion protection to prevent accidental destruction:
resource "aws_db_instance" "this" {
  deletion_protection = true
}
For S3, remove `force_destroy = true`. For EC2, set `disable_api_termination = true`.
